/ML, analytics, EDA, HPC, media, genomics, or financial trading. Not applicable for SQL query engines (Athena, Spark, Redshift, EMR), ETL (Glue), streaming (Kafka, MSK, Kinesis), or managed database services (RDS, Aurora, DynamoDB).\n\nServices: s3, efs, ebs, fsx\nTasks: decide, configure, create, optimize\nPersona: developer, architect, devops, it-administrator, storage-administrator, systems-engineer\nWorkload: storage","skill_name":"aws-storage"},{"rank_order":3,"title":"recovery-controller-setup","skill_description":"Configures AWS Application Recovery Controller (ARC) for operational resilience: routing controls with safety rules for cross-Region failover, and zonal shift / zonal autoshift for AZ-impairment recovery. Applies when setting up failover routing, configuring safety rules, enabling zonal shift, or configuring zonal autoshift with practice runs. Also applies when shifting traffic out of a specific Availability Zone (AZ) for an ALB/NLB or other resource. For a broader \"an AZ is impaired, what is my response across services\" question, see aws-resilience-lifecycle. Does not apply to Resilience Hub setup or FIS experiments.\n\n\nServices: route53-recovery-control-config, arc-zonal-shift\nTasks: configure, deploy\nPersona: developer, devops, sre\nWorkload: resilience\n*","skill_name":"recovery-controller-setup"}]}}"}]}], "label": "Verify whether AWS Backup supports ElastiCache Valkey/Redis replication groups", "parent_id": "c9bddd12-89aa-4041-8758-ededc1e834e5"}

